      ],
      "source": "https://www.eastlongisland.com/jamesport/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 19th century, fishermen harvested menhaden—called bunkers—processing them into oil for lamps and paint, with catches reaching hundreds of thousands.",
